{"content":[{"c":["SHAMIR (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of the 11 towns in the hill country allotted to Judah. First in the list of towns, Shamir is followed by Jattir (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.48","r":"Josh.15.48","rawR":"Josh.15.48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.48","value":"Josh.15.48"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:48"},"). Its location is perhaps at el-Bireh, about 12 miles (19.3 kilometers) southwest of Hebron."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Town where Tola the judge lived and was later buried. Shamir was in the land of Ephraim (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.10.1-2","r":"Judg.10.1-2","rawR":"Judg.10.1-2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.10.1-2","value":"Judg.10.1-2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 10:1-2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ShamirPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:48","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.48","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.48","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.48"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 10:1-2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.10.1-2","rawQueryValue":"Judg.10.1-2","sourceRefExact":"Judg.10.1-2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"962b7af48a095c2cf37a879f685794506ddb0e881d70aab4706c9b56c4372f2f","sourceItemName":"ShamirPlace","sourceItemOrder":202,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ShamirPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shamir (Place)","title":"Shamir (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}